      "text": "\n\nA computer works by using a combination of hardware and software components to process, store, and communicate data. The hardware components of a computer include the central processing unit (CPU), memory (RAM), storage devices (hard drive, solid state drive, etc.), and input/output (I/O) devices (keyboard, mouse, monitor, etc.).\n\nThe CPU is the \"brain\" of the computer, responsible for executing instructions and performing calculations. It is made up of several components, including the control unit, arithmetic logic unit (ALU), and registers. The control unit retrieves instructions from memory and decides which operations to perform, while the ALU performs mathematical and logical operations on data. Registers are small amounts of memory built into the CPU that hold data temporarily while it is being processed.\n\nMemory (RAM) is a temporary storage area where the computer stores data and instructions while they are being used. It is called \"random access\" because the computer can access any location in the memory directly, rather than having to read the data in a particular order. Storage devices, such as hard drives and solid state drives, are used to store data and programs permanently.\n\nInput/output (I/O)"
